    "updated_at": "2018-09-05T20:40:28Z",
    "body": "> What Firefox does is that when doing a [[Call]] it will replace the global with the WindowProxy for the `this` value _unless_ the call is to a WebIDL-defined getter/setter/method. It sounds like Chrome is doing the same but across the board?\r\n\r\nYeah, that seems like the case without getting too deep into the code. I also conjecture that there is a piece of code somewhere in Chromium for Web IDL calls that eventually unwraps `WindowProxy` down to the original `Window` but I'm not sure how that works.",
